---
// The site's icon <link>s, shared by every <head>. Two heads exist and must
// stay in step: Layout.astro (all content pages) and pages/index.astro (the
// maze, which deliberately does NOT use Layout, so it cannot inherit them).
// Keeping the set here means a future addition (a manifest, a mask-icon, a
// second apple-touch size) lands on both by construction rather than by memory.
//
// Order matters. Browsers that support SVG favicons match the first link and
// use that one file at EVERY size, so favicon.svg is the one that has to stay
// legible in a 16px tab; the .ico is only ever fetched by browsers that do not
// (Safari, mainly), which is why it carries just 16 and 32.
//
// No `?url` import here, unlike CjkFonts/KatexStyles: these are stable paths in
// public/ that outside agents (a browser's default /favicon.ico probe, the iOS
// home screen) look up by name, so they must not be content-hashed.
---

<link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
<link rel="icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="16x16 32x32" />
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/apple-touch-icon.png" />
